{"abstract":"The generalized uncertainty relation applicable to quantum and stochastic systems is derived within the stochastic variational method. This relation not only reproduces the well-known inequality in quantum mechanics but also is applicable to the Gross-Pitaevskii equation and the Navier-Stokes-Fourier equation, showing that the finite minimum uncertainty between the position and the momentum is not an inherent property of quantum mechanics but a common feature of stochastic systems. We further discuss the possible implication of the present study in discussing the application of the hydrodynamic picture to microscopic systems, like relativistic heavy-ion collisions.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"1208.0258","authors":["T. Koide","T. Kodama"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-18T21:58:06+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1208.0258.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":11,"pdf_bytes":611400,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"4bec7b610a78ef96eef841f908a5aae7785ee823970b260fa79e4f3b625edc2a","created_at":"2026-08-18T21:58:06+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"763b6ca3868b0af2770ec79b8ae31e3ebadb1cf6fbccc084d738761ccb8b2256","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"Generalization of Uncertainty Relation for Quantum and Stochastic Systems","updated_at":"2026-08-18T21:58:06+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-C543EED472C3","year":2012}
